  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Substrate recognition component of a SCF (SKP1-CUL1-F-box protein) E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase complex which mediates the ubiquitination and subsequent proteasomal degradation of target proteins. Recognizes and binds to phosphorylated target proteins. SCF(BTRC) mediates the ubiquitination of CTNNB1 and participates in Wnt signaling. SCF(BTRC) mediates the ubiquitination of phosphorylated NFKBIA (I\u03baB\u03b1), NFKBIB, NFKBIE, ATF4, CDC25A, FBXO5/EMI1, SNAI1, SMAD3, SMAD4, PER1, PER2, and REST, thereby playing roles in NF-\u03baB signaling, cell cycle regulation, circadian clock, epithelial-mesenchymal transition, and TGF-\u03b2 signaling.",
    "catalytic_activity": "Functions as substrate receptor for E3 ubiquitin ligase complex; does not have intrinsic catalytic activity but confers substrate specificity",
    "subcellular_location": [
      "Nucleus",
      "Cytoplasm",
      "Nucleoplasm",
      "Plasma membrane",
      "Cytosol"
    ],
    "tissue_specificity": "Widely expressed with high levels in brain, heart, and testis. Undetectable in small intestine and thymus. Cell type enrichment in astrocytes, neurons, microglia, and granulosa cells",
