    "pathway_role_summary": "BTRC is a critical E3 ubiquitin ligase substrate receptor that regulates multiple signaling pathways by targeting phosphorylated proteins for proteasomal degradation. Key roles include: (1) Wnt signaling - degrades phosphorylated beta-catenin to prevent inappropriate pathway activation; (2) NF-\u03baB signaling - degrades I\u03baB inhibitors to allow NF-\u03baB nuclear translocation; (3) Cell cycle - degrades CDC25A, WEE1, EMI1 at checkpoints; (4) Circadian clock - degrades PER proteins for oscillatory rhythms; (5) TGF-\u03b2 signaling - degrades SMAD proteins; (6) EMT regulation - degrades SNAI1 transcription factor"
  },
