    "data_quality_notes": "High quality data available from multiple sources. Extensive experimental characterization of substrate interactions and binding affinities. Crystal structures available for substrate-bound complexes. Some kinetic parameters (kon/koff) not available for most interactions. Isoform 1 sequence not fully provided but well-characterized as 36 amino acids shorter than canonical isoform 2.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "BTRC is essential for modeling Wnt, NF-\u03baB, cell cycle, and circadian signaling pathways. It acts as a phosphorylation-dependent switch that converts kinase signaling into protein degradation. Critical quantitative parameters available: beta-catenin binding Kd ~1 nM, I\u03baB\u03b1 binding Kd ~26 nM. Substrate recognition requires prior phosphorylation by pathway-specific kinases (GSK3B, CK1, IKK, CHK1), creating temporal regulatory logic. Homodimerization adds cooperative binding effects. The protein integrates multiple signaling inputs and converts them to ubiquitination outputs, making it a key regulatory node."
  }
